# ACCESSIBILITY GUARDIAN: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

## 1. SEMANTIC HTML — Zero Div Buttons
```tsx
// ❌ REJECTED — div with onClick and no accessibility
<div onClick={handleClick}>Submit</div>

// ✅ REQUIRED — proper button with keyboard support
<button type="button" onClick={handleClick}>Submit</button>
// OR if truly custom:
<div role="button" tabIndex={0} onClick={handleClick} onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Enter' && handleClick()}>
```
- All `<img>` must have `alt`. Decorative images: `alt=""`.
- Use `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<article>`, `<section>` — not `<div>` wrappers.

## 2. ARIA REQUIREMENTS
| Element | Required ARIA |
|---|---|
| Icon-only button | `aria-label="Description"` |
| Input field | `<label htmlFor="id">` + matching `id` on input |
| Modal/Dialog | `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"` + `aria-labelledby` |
| Loading state | `aria-busy="true"` on container |
| Error message | `role="alert"` on error container |

## 3. KEYBOARD NAVIGATION
- All interactive elements reachable via `Tab`.
- Modal open: focus trapped inside. Modal close: focus returns to trigger.
- Dropdown: `ArrowUp`/`ArrowDown` to navigate, `Escape` to close.
- Skip-to-main link: first focusable element on every page.

## 4. COLOR & CONTRAST
- **Body text**: ≥ 4.5:1 contrast ratio (WCAG AA).
- **Large text / UI components**: ≥ 3:1 contrast ratio.
- **Never convey information via color alone** — pair with icon or text label.

## 5. MOTION SAFETY
```tsx
// ✅ Respect user preference
<motion.div
  animate={{ opacity: 1 }}
  transition={
    prefersReducedMotion ? { duration: 0 } : { type: "spring", stiffness: 100 }
  }
/>
```
- Wrap all Framer Motion animations with `prefers-reduced-motion` checks.
